{"id":"e09t2","name":"Valid Flight Connections","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","flights_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A travel website proposes itineraries with one connection. <code>flights_df</code> has the columns <code>flight_id</code> (string), <code>origin</code>, <code>destination</code> (strings, airport codes), <code>departs_at</code>, <code>arrives_at</code> (timestamps) and <code>status</code> (<code>\"scheduled\"</code> or <code>\"cancelled\"</code>).</p>\n<p>A <b>connection</b> is a pair of two different scheduled flights <code>(first, second)</code> where:</p>\n<ul><li>the second flight leaves from the airport where the first one lands;</li><li>the layover, <code>second.departs_at - first.arrives_at</code>, is between <code>45</code> and <code>240</code> minutes, both included;</li><li>the second flight does <b>not</b> go back to the origin of the first flight.</li></ul>\n<p>Airport codes must be trimmed and upper-cased. Your task is to return the columns <code>first_flight</code>, <code>second_flight</code>, <code>origin</code>, <code>via</code>, <code>destination</code> and <code>layover_min</code> (long), sorted by <code>origin</code>, <code>destination</code>, <code>layover_min</code>, then <code>first_flight</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>flights_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>flight_id</th><th>origin</th><th>destination</th><th>departs_at</th><th>arrives_at</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>AT1</td><td>LFW</td><td>CMN</td><td>2026-03-01 06:00:00</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>AT2</td><td>CMN</td><td>CDG</td><td>2026-03-01 10:45:00</td><td>2026-03-01 14:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>AT3</td><td>cmn </td><td>LFW</td><td>2026-03-01 11:00:00</td><td>2026-03-01 15:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>AT4</td><td>CMN</td><td>JFK</td><td>2026-03-01 14:00:00</td><td>2026-03-01 22:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>AT5</td><td>CMN</td><td>DSS</td><td>2026-03-01 14:01:00</td><td>2026-03-01 17:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>AT6</td><td>CMN</td><td>MAD</td><td>2026-03-01 12:00:00</td><td>2026-03-01 13:30:00</td><td>cancelled</td></tr><tr><td>AT7</td><td>CMN</td><td>LHR</td><td>2026-03-01 10:30:00</td><td>2026-03-01 13:00:00</td><td>scheduled</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>first_flight</th><th>second_flight</th><th>origin</th><th>via</th><th>destination</th><th>layover_min</th></tr><tr><td>AT1</td><td>AT2</td><td>LFW</td><td>CMN</td><td>CDG</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>AT1</td><td>AT4</td><td>LFW</td><td>CMN</td><td>JFK</td><td>240</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, flights_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return flights_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["auto-jointure","condition sur le temps","alias","exclure les annulés"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"flights_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"flight_id string, origin string, destination string, departs_at timestamp, arrives_at timestamp, status string","rows":[["AT1","LFW","CMN","2026-03-01 06:00:00","2026-03-01 10:00:00","scheduled"],["AT2","CMN","CDG","2026-03-01 10:45:00","2026-03-01 14:00:00","scheduled"],["AT3","cmn ","LFW","2026-03-01 11:00:00","2026-03-01 15:00:00","scheduled"],["AT4","CMN","JFK","2026-03-01 14:00:00","2026-03-01 22:00:00","scheduled"],["AT5","CMN","DSS","2026-03-01 14:01:00","2026-03-01 17:00:00","scheduled"],["AT6","CMN","MAD","2026-03-01 12:00:00","2026-03-01 13:30:00","cancelled"],["AT7","CMN","LHR","2026-03-01 10:30:00","2026-03-01 13:00:00","scheduled"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["first_flight","second_flight","origin","via","destination","layover_min"],"rows":[["AT1","AT2","LFW","CMN","CDG",45],["AT1"